From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 04:38:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10597/11362] Record that agents run the RED full suite because
 our own docs prescribe it

Appended to the 2026-08-24 suite-is-RED entry rather than opening a new one: that
entry says it is "where the signal now lives until it has a proper home", and this
is the same signal with a cause attached.

Observed 06:00-08:00Z. Two consecutive conductor children each ran the full suite,
about 2.5 hours of conductor slot between them, reaching 25% and then 59%, with the
agent narrating unrelated failures the whole way.

The cause is not agent misbehaviour. Zero of milestone 2026.09.598's 13 prompts ask
for a full-suite pytest -- the one test mention is a scoped path -- but CLAUDE.md's
Build/Test/Deploy section prescribes `pytest tests/python` with coverage. The agent
called it "the required command" and was reasonable to.

So two layers of our own instructions disagree. The harness refuses this command
deliberately: run_tests(full=False) at every call site, two commented "full suite
hangs". The documentation still prescribes it. An agent following the written verify
step does exactly what the harness avoids as unsafe.

The documented form is additionally unusable: it carries --cov, and pytest under
coverage aborts on this repository with exit 134 from JAX/absl double-init. This
agent dropped --cov on its own, which is the only reason it reached 59% rather than
dying at the start.

Base rate stated in the entry rather than implied: 100 full-suite narration lines in
24 hours, all inside three consecutive hours. A concentrated current episode, not
established as chronic. It should not be quoted as a daily cost until more days are
counted.

No fix attempted. CLAUDE.md is operator-curated, so reconciling the two layers is an
operator decision; the entry lists the three candidate resolutions and leaves the
choice open.

